    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d453">

                <pb facs="0566" n="556" xml:id="pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2148: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-21T15:00:00+09:00">June 21, 1948—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 21—6:36 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1103. Embassy sees no objection to changes proposed by NAC for article VII
                    (reDeptel 900, June 19, 10 a.m.). Reference Deptel has been repeated by Embassy
                    to Shanghai for Lapham who presumably will comment to you directly.<anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d453-f1"/></p>
                <p>Repeated Shanghai 500.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
